.TH MAKEKEEPER 1 "October 2026" "makekeeper 1.0.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
makekeeper \- a safer installer and manager for Makefile-based Linux applications

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B makekeeper
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.br
.B makekeeper
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help | \-v | \-\-version ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B makekeeper
installs applications that ship with nothing but a Makefile, and keeps a registry
of everything it installed so packages can be listed, updated and uninstalled later.

Packages can come from the curated package catalog, a Git URL, or a local directory.
Git packages are cloned as your user into
.IR ~/.local/share/makekeeper/sources/<name>/
and built with
.BR make (1)
as your user. Only
.B make install
and
.B make uninstall
run as root, through a small helper that is authorized with
.BR pkexec (1).
polkit remembers the authorization briefly, so one command asks for your password once.

.SH COMMANDS
Every command also accepts
.B \-h
or
.B \-\-help
as its first argument to show help for that command.

.TP
.BI install " NAME" | URL | DIR " \fR[\fB\-\-name \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-override\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR]"
Install a package. A
.I NAME
is looked up in the synced package catalog, a
.I URL
is cloned, and a
.I DIR
is built in place. The project is built with
.B make
(skipped when a
.IR build/ ,
.I target/
or
.I bin/
directory already exists), installed with
.BR "make install" ,
and recorded in the registry. Before building, it shows the package, its source and what
will run as root, and asks for confirmation.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
Register the package under
.I NAME
instead of the catalog, repository or directory name.
.TP
.B \-\-override
Reinstall a package that is already installed, removing its previously tracked files first.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Don't ask for confirmation. Required when there is no terminal to ask on, such as in scripts.
.RE

.TP
.BI uninstall " NAME" " \fR[\fB\-\-yes\fR]"
Run the package's
.BR "make uninstall" ,
remove the files and symlinks the registry tracks for it, delete the clone MakeKeeper made,
and remove it from the registry. Directories you installed from are never deleted.
It lists what will be removed and asks for confirmation first.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Don't ask for confirmation. Required when there is no terminal to ask on, such as in scripts.
.RE

.TP
.BR update " [\fINAME\fR]"
Fetch the package's Git repository and, if there are new commits or the installed commit
differs, pull, rebuild and reinstall it. Without
.IR NAME ,
every package installed from Git is updated.

.TP
.B list
List installed packages with their URL, install date and commit.

.TP
.BI info " NAME"
Show an installed package's URL, source directory, commit, install date and tracked files.

.TP
.BI search " QUERY"
Search the package catalog's names and descriptions, ignoring case.

.TP
.B sync
Download the latest package catalog and look up each package's latest version.
Required before installing or searching by catalog name.

.TP
.B fetch
Print package statistics as
.IR installed / git ,
the number of installed packages and how many of them came from Git.

.TP
.B gui
Launch the graphical interface.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the list of commands.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version.

.SH EXAMPLES
Sync the catalog and find a package:
.RS
.PP
.nf
makekeeper sync
makekeeper search terminal
.fi
.RE

Install from the catalog, a Git URL, or a local directory:
.RS
.PP
.nf
makekeeper install st
makekeeper install https://github.com/user/project.git
makekeeper install ~/src/project
.fi
.RE

Install under a custom name, or reinstall:
.RS
.PP
.nf
makekeeper install ~/src/project \-\-name myapp
makekeeper install st \-\-override
.fi
.RE

Update one package, or all of them:
.RS
.PP
.nf
makekeeper update st
makekeeper update
.fi
.RE

Uninstall a package:
.RS
.PP
.nf
makekeeper uninstall st
.fi
.RE

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/makekeeper/registry.json
Registry of installed packages.
.TP
.I /var/lib/makekeeper/cache/packages.json
Synced package catalog.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/makekeeper/sources/<name>/
Your clones of Git-based packages, deleted on uninstall.
.TP
.I ~/.config/makekeeper/settings.conf
GUI settings.
.TP
.I <prefix>/lib/makekeeper/makekeeper\-helper
The privileged helper; the only part of MakeKeeper that runs as root.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit\-1/actions/io.github.creativecodecat.makekeeper.policy
polkit policy that authorizes the helper.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to a non-empty value, disable coloured output. Output is also plain when it is not a terminal.
.TP
.BR XDG_DATA_HOME ", " XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Override the locations of the sources directory and the settings file.

.SH SECURITY
A Makefile can run any command, and
.B make install
runs as root. Only install projects you trust, and read their Makefile first.
Builds are not sandboxed. The helper only accepts a fixed set of operations: running
.BR make ,
.BR "make install" ,
.B make uninstall
or
.B make clean
in a project, removing files the registry tracks, and writing MakeKeeper's own state.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR make (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR pkexec (1)

.SH AUTHOR
CreativeCodeCat and MakeKeeper contributors.
